>Q5ZRQ0 name=lubX | gene=lubX;legU2;lpg2830 | locus=lpg2830 | protein_name=E3 ubiquitin-protein ligase LubX | organism=Legionella pneumophila subsp. pneumophila (strain Philadelphia 1 / ATCC 33152 / DSM 7513) | taxid=272624 | reviewed=true | evidence=experimentally_supported | evidence_reference=https://doi.org/10.1038/s44320-024-00076-z | source=UniProt;Pathogens3D | annotation=Effector proteins function to alter host cell physiology and promote bacterial survival in host tissues. This protein is an E3 ubiquitin ligase that interferes with host's ubiquitination pathway. Acts in conjunction with host E2 ubiquitin-conjugating enzymes UBE2D1 (UBCH5A) or UBE2D3 (UBCH5C), and mediates polyubiquitination of host kinase CLK1 / Pathogens3D: LubX effector. E3 ubiquitin-protein ligase. Its N terminus activates an extended number of ubiquitin-conjugating (E2) enzymes including UBE2W, UBEL6, and all tested members of UBE2D and UBE2E families {PMID: 26146184}. Structurally characterized {PDB: 4wz3}.
