>Q5ZTK6 name=sidJ | gene=sidJ;lpg2155;SidJ | locus=lpg2155 | protein_name=Calmodulin-dependent glutamylase SidJ | organism=Legionella pneumophila subsp. pneumophila (strain Philadelphia 1 / ATCC 33152 / DSM 7513) | taxid=272624 | reviewed=true | evidence=experimentally_supported | evidence_reference=https://doi.org/10.1038/s44320-024-00076-z | source=UniProt;Pathogens3D | annotation=Glutamylase that mediates the covalent attachment of glutamate moieties to SdeA on one of the catalytic residues that is required for its mono-ADP-ribosyltransferase activity (PubMed:31330531, PubMed:31330532). In turn, inhibits SdeA ubiquitinating activity. Also glutamylates related SdeB, SdeC and SidE (PubMed:31123136, PubMed:31330531). Glutamylase activity only occurs in the host since it requires host calmodulin (PubMed:28497808, PubMed:31123136, PubMed:31330531, PubMed:31330532). May also reverse the SdeA-mediated substrate ubiquitination by cleaving the phosphodiester bond that links phosphoribosylated ubiquitin to protein substrates via its deubiquitinase activity (PubMed:28497808) / Pathogens3D: SidJ pseudokinase that catalyzes protein polyglutamylation to inhibit the SidE-family ubiquitin ligases {PMID: 34407442, 31330531}. Structurally characterized {PDB: 6k4l, 6oqq, 7mis, 6k4r, 7mir, 6s5t, 6plm, 7ppo}
